=> Service Bus Queues

    -> What is a Queue?
        - Provides FIFO (First In First Out) message delivery
        - One or more competing consumers can process messages
        - Only one consumer processes each message

        Example:
            Producer ---> Queue ---> One Consumer

    -> FIFO Behavior
        - Messages are processed in the same order they are added

        Example:
            Added:
                Message1
                Message2
                Message3

            Received:
                Message1
                Message2
                Message3

    -> Durable Message Storage
        - Messages are stored safely inside queue
        - Producer and consumer do not need to run simultaneously

        Example:
            - Producer sends message at 10 AM
            - Consumer processes message at 11 AM

    -> Loose Coupling
        - Producer and consumer are independent
        - Changes in consumer do not affect producer

        Benefits:
            - Easier upgrades
            - Better maintainability
            - Better scalability

    -> Load Leveling

        -> Problem
            - System traffic varies over time
            - Consumers may not handle peak traffic directly

        -> Solution
            - Queue acts as a buffer

        Example:
            High Traffic
                -> Messages stored in queue
                -> Consumers process gradually

        -> Benefit
            - Consumer handles average load instead of peak load

    -> Queue Creation Methods
        - Azure Portal
        - PowerShell
        - Azure CLI
        - ARM Templates

    -> Supported Client Languages
        - C#
        - Java
        - Python
        - JavaScript

