=> Service Bus Receive Modes

    -> Two Receive Modes
        - Receive and Delete
        - Peek Lock

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Receive and Delete Mode

    -> Working
        - Service Bus immediately marks message as consumed
        - Message is removed before processing completes

        Flow:
            Receive Request
                -> Message Deleted
                -> Message Returned to Consumer

    -> Advantage
        - Simple and fast

    -> Risk
        - Message loss possible during failure

        Example:
            - Consumer receives message
            - Application crashes before processing
            - Message already deleted
            - Message permanently lost

    -> Best Use Cases
        - Non-critical processing
        - Logging
        - Temporary notifications

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Peek Lock Mode

    -> Working
        - Message is first locked
        - Other consumers cannot access it
        - Message removed only after successful processing

        Flow:
            Receive Message
                -> Lock Message
                -> Process Message
                -> Complete Message
                -> Delete Message

    -> Advantage
        - Prevents message loss
        - Safer processing model

    -> Abandon Scenario
        - Consumer can abandon message
        - Message becomes available again

        Example:
            Processing Failed
                -> Abandon Message
                -> Queue Unlocks Message
                -> Another Consumer Processes It

    -> Lock Timeout
        - Lock exists only for limited duration
        - If processing exceeds timeout:
            - Message becomes available again

    -> Best Use Cases
        - Critical business operations
        - Payment processing
        - Order processing
        - Banking systems

