=> Topics and Subscriptions

    -> Purpose
        - Supports Publish-Subscribe (Pub/Sub) model
        - Enables one-to-many communication

    -> Queue vs Topic

        Queue:
            - One message -> One consumer

        Topic:
            - One message -> Multiple subscribers

    -> Publish Subscribe Architecture

        Example:

                Publisher
                    |
                  Topic
                /   |   \
               /    |    \
         SubscriptionA
         SubscriptionB
         SubscriptionC

    -> How It Works
        - Publisher sends message to topic
        - Topic distributes copies to subscriptions
        - Consumers read from subscriptions

    -> Subscription
        - Acts like a virtual queue
        - Stores copy of topic messages

    -> Benefits
        - Massive scalability
        - Multiple services can consume same event
        - Better event-driven architecture

    -> Supported Patterns
        - Competing Consumers
        - Temporal Decoupling
        - Load Leveling
        - Load Balancing

====================================================================================================
=> Rules and Actions

    -> Purpose
        - Allows selective message processing
        - Different subscribers can receive different messages

    -> Message Filtering
        - Subscriptions can filter messages using properties

        Example:
            OrderType = Electronics
            StoreName = DelhiStore

    -> Filter Types
        - System Properties
            Example:
                - Label

        - Custom Application Properties
            Example:
                - StoreName
                - OrderType

    -> SQL Filter Expressions
        - Used to define filtering conditions

        Example:
            StoreName = 'DelhiStore'

    -> Actions
        - Modify message properties during filtering

    -> Important Point
        - If no SQL filter exists:
            - Action applies to all messages

