=> Explore Azure Queue Storage

    -> What is Azure Queue Storage?
        - Azure Queue Storage is a service for storing large numbers of messages
        - Used for asynchronous communication between applications/services
        - Commonly used for background processing

    -> Purpose of Azure Queue Storage
        - Create backlog of work
        - Process tasks asynchronously
        - Decouple producer and consumer applications
        - Improve scalability and reliability

    -> Communication Protocols
        - Accessible globally using:
            - HTTP
            - HTTPS

        - Access requires authenticated requests

    -> Message Characteristics
        - Maximum message size:
            - 64 KB

        - Queue can contain:
            - Millions of messages

        - Total storage depends on:
            - Storage account capacity

====================================================================================================
=> Components of Azure Queue Storage

    -> Main Components
        - Storage Account
        - Queue
        - Message
        - Queue URL

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Storage Account

    -> Definition
        - Main Azure resource that contains storage services
        - All Queue Storage operations occur inside storage account

    -> Purpose
        - Provides access control
        - Stores queues and messages
        - Defines total storage capacity

    -> Important Point
        - Without storage account, queues cannot exist

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Queue

    -> Definition
        - Queue stores collection of messages

    -> Purpose
        - Temporarily stores work/tasks until processed

    -> Important Rules
        - All messages must belong to a queue
        - Queue name must be lowercase

        Valid Example:
            imagesqueue

        Invalid Example:
            ImagesQueue

    -> Queue Behavior
        - Producer adds messages
        - Consumer retrieves and processes messages

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Message

    -> Definition
        - Unit of data stored inside queue

    -> Message Content
        - Can contain any format of data

        Examples:
            - JSON
            - XML
            - Plain Text

    -> Maximum Size
        - Up to 64 KB

    -> Time-To-Live (TTL)

        -> Before Version 2017-07-29
            - Maximum TTL:
                - 7 days

        -> Version 2017-07-29 or Later
            - TTL can be:
                - Any positive value
                - -1 (Never expire)

        -> Default TTL
            - 7 days

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=> Queue URL Format

    -> Queue Address Format

        https://<storage-account>.queue.core.windows.net/<queue-name>

    -> Example

        https://myaccount.queue.core.windows.net/images-to-download

    -> URL Parts

        https://
            - Secure communication protocol

        myaccount
            - Storage account name

        queue.core.windows.net
            - Azure Queue Storage endpoint

        images-to-download
            - Queue name

====================================================================================================
=> Queue Storage Workflow

    -> Step 1
        - Producer sends message to queue

    -> Step 2
        - Queue stores message safely

    -> Step 3
        - Consumer retrieves message later

    -> Step 4
        - Consumer processes task asynchronously

    Example:

        Producer
            -> Queue Storage
                -> Worker/Consumer

